      <h2 id="what-collagen-can-do">What can a collagen supplement actually do?</h2>
      <p>It can support skin quality while you deal with skin quantity another way. Conflating those two outcomes is how this category oversells itself.</p>
      <p>Hydration, elasticity and tone are what the peptide trials measure, and they are reasonable things to support after weight loss, when skin often looks dull and crepey as well as loose. Expect that on the <a href="/pages/how-long-does-collagen-take-to-work">8 to 12 week timeline</a> most trials used, and expect no reduction in the surface area of skin on your abdomen or arms.</p>
      <p>One caveat matters more during weight loss than at any other time. Collagen is an incomplete protein: it lacks tryptophan and is low in leucine, the amino acid that drives muscle protein synthesis, and whey produces a greater muscle protein synthesis response head to head. Count the 8g of protein in a daily shot as collagen, not as the protein protecting your lean mass in a deficit. We compare them in <a href="/pages/collagen-vs-whey-protein">collagen vs whey protein</a>.</p>

