      <h2 id="doctor">When to see a doctor</h2>
      <p>Some of this needs a clinician rather than a supplement.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Recurrent rash or infection in a skin fold.</strong> Intertrigo that keeps returning in an abdominal or thigh fold needs treating, and is a recognised reason to discuss contouring.</li>
        <li><strong>Skin breakdown, ulceration or odour from a fold.</strong> See a doctor promptly rather than managing it at home.</li>
        <li><strong>Weight loss you did not intend.</strong> That is a symptom to investigate, not a cosmetic problem.</li>
        <li><strong>Before any contouring surgery.</strong> These procedures carry real risks, including thromboembolism, and belong with a qualified plastic surgeon who checks weight stability and nutrition first.</li>
      </ul>

